
# 🚀 Cursor Prompt — Full Clerk Protection (Detailed + Production Ready)

I have a **Next.js 14+ App Router project** and I want to fully protect my entire application using **Clerk authentication**.

My goal is:

🔒 No user should be able to access any page of the app without signing in.
👤 When a visitor enters the site, they must be redirected to `/sign-in`.
✅ After successful authentication, they can access the app.
🚫 No default Clerk header UI should be rendered.
✨ The authentication UI must be clean and production-ready.

---

## 🎯 Requirements

Please implement the complete authentication setup with the following structure and best practices:

---

## 1️⃣ Configure ClerkProvider

Update `app/layout.tsx`:

* Wrap the entire application with `<ClerkProvider>`
* Keep the HTML structure valid
* Do not introduce unnecessary re-renders
* Follow Next.js App Router best practices

Expected structure:

* `<ClerkProvider>`
* `<html>`
* `<body>`
* `{children}`

---

## 2️⃣ Create Authentication Routes

Create the following routes exactly:

### ✅ `app/sign-in/[[...sign-in]]/page.tsx`

* Render `<SignIn />` from `@clerk/nextjs`
* Ensure proper full-page rendering

### ✅ `app/sign-up/[[...sign-up]]/page.tsx`

* Render `<SignUp />` from `@clerk/nextjs`
* Ensure proper full-page rendering

Do not wrap these unnecessarily.
Keep them clean.

---

## 3️⃣ Create `middleware.ts` in Root

Create a `middleware.ts` file that:

* Uses `clerkMiddleware` from `@clerk/nextjs/server`
* Protects ALL routes
* Makes ONLY:

  * `/sign-in`
  * `/sign-up`
    public
* Automatically redirects unauthenticated users to sign-in
* Uses proper route matching
* Avoids breaking static assets and `_next` files

The middleware must be production-ready and correctly configured.

---

## 4️⃣ Enforce Full App Protection

Authentication flow must work like this:

Visitor enters `/`
→ Automatically redirected to `/sign-in`
→ After successful login
→ Redirected back to app
→ Full access granted

If logged out:
→ Access denied
→ Redirected again

No page should be accessible without login.

---

## 5️⃣ Navbar Integration

Inside my existing custom Navbar component:

* Import and render `<UserButton />`
* Only show it when the user is authenticated
* Add `afterSignOutUrl="/sign-in"`
* Do NOT render `<SignInButton />` or `<SignUpButton />`
* Do NOT render Clerk’s default header

Keep navbar integration clean and minimal.

---

## 6️⃣ Production Quality Standards

Make sure:

* Code follows Next.js App Router best practices
* No deprecated Clerk APIs
* No console warnings
* Clean folder structure
* Proper TypeScript usage (if project uses TS)
* No unnecessary client components unless required

---

## 7️⃣ Environment Variables

Assume `.env.local` already contains:

NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
CLERK_SECRET_KEY

Do not regenerate them.

---

## 🎯 Final Result Must Achieve:

* Entire app protected
* Automatic redirect if unauthenticated
* Clean authentication pages
* Profile button in navbar when logged in
* No UI flashes of protected content
* Production-ready implementation

---

Generate all necessary files and modifications.

